      "retrieved": "2026-10-10",
      "note": "v1 line pinned: tag v1.18.35 -> commit 53d1eabb61e21162157817bf677da0a4ad3332e3; loader packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts. The v2 dev line (HEAD 7b3d4ce3a7dbd2a6d3637722a0d5f22a7d086937, shipped as @opencode/cli 2.0.26) is out of scope for this adapter. Note (2026-10-11): the sst/opencode org was renamed and now redirects to anomalyco/opencode; the same tag -> commit still resolves."
    },
    {
      "id": "OC-CONFIGDIR-SOURCE-20261011",
      "kind": "source-code",
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sst/opencode/53d1eabb61e21162157817bf677da0a4ad3332e3/packages/opencode/src/config/paths.ts",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-11",
      "note": "Read at the pinned commit 53d1eabb61e21162157817bf677da0a4ad3332e3. paths.ts `directories()` returns `unique([Global.Path.config, ...project .opencode dirs, ...home .opencode, ...(Flag.OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR ? [Flag.OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR] : [])])` — the env value is a DIRECTORY appended last. config/config.ts then, inside its directories loop, loads `opencode.json` followed by `opencode.jsonc` from every directory that `endsWith(\".opencode\")` or `=== Flag.OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR`; the loop runs after the project files are merged and before `$OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT`, and the layer is skipped entirely when `Flag.OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR` is unset. Consequences encoded in this registry: the sources are the two files inside the directory (jsonc wins as it is merged second), a file-valued env var contributes nothing, and the placement rank 45 between `oc.opencode_dirs` (40) and `oc.inline` (50) is source-verified. Raw transcript: docs/research/evidence/opencode-config-dir-20261011.txt"
    },
    {
      "id": "OC-PROJECT-SOURCE-20261011",
      "kind": "source-code",
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sst/opencode/53d1eabb61e21162157817bf677da0a4ad3332e3/packages/opencode/src/config/paths.ts",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-11",
      "note": "Read at the pinned commit 53d1eabb61e21162157817bf677da0a4ad3332e3. paths.ts `ConfigPaths.files(name, directory, worktree?)` calls `FSUtil.up({ targets: [`${name}.jsonc`, `${name}.json`], start: directory (= the working directory), stop: worktree (= the repository root) })` and returns its result `.toReversed()`. The callee is `packages/core/src/fs-util.ts`: `up()` pushes a match at EVERY level from `start` upward while `options.stop !== current` (and stops at the filesystem root when no stop is reached), so `files()` yields every ancestor `opencode.json`/`opencode.jsonc` from the working directory up to the worktree, outermost first and working directory last; `config/config.ts` merges them in that order, so the NEAREST file wins and every ancestor contributes. configlens therefore walks `ctx.cwd` -> boundary inclusive and emits each level's `opencode.json` then `opencode.jsonc` as `oc.project` candidates outermost-first, so the engine's last-definition-wins tie-break selects the nearest file. Boundary = `--project-root` when supplied, otherwise the nearest git root; with no boundary only `ctx.cwd` is read and the boundary-uncertain signal is kept. (Kills audit finding A3.)"
    }
  ],
